  "content": {
    "_uid": "8216af4a-c655-ed8a-1c40-321c7e50f5fd",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "66b6d9d4-2e5b-299a-ea21-09e170e0dc99",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The Hospital has had two confirmed deaths over the past three weeks due to the Congo virus. One of these, an AKUH nursing assistant, was corroborated by the Center for Disease Control and Prevention in Atlanta, USA. This nursing aide had been caring for a patient who was later clinically confirmed to have also died from the Congo virus.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Four patients currently admitted to AKUH are under evaluation and are being closely monitored. None of the patients are in a critical condition, including a heath care worker from AKUH, who is making a satisfactory recovery. AKUH has arranged the testing of blood samples of all these four patients by the Center for Disease Control and Prevention in Atlanta to rule out the possibility of CCHF.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
