    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\"There have been no new cases of the Congo Crimean Hemorrhagic Fever (CCHF) at the Aga Khan University Hospital (AKUH),\" said Dr Arif Rashid Sarwari, Assistant Professor, Department of Medicine, and AKUH. The Hospital has been treating patients with Viral Hemorrhagic Fevers (VHF) for over five years. The Congo virus, a variety of VHF, is a seasonal illness, with cases most often reported from September to December Dr Sarwari also stressed that \"the Congo virus is not an airborne disease, and is contracted through tick bite and exposure to an infected animal or infected patient's blood or body fluid secretions.\"",
